-- what must be served
ok   a file in the root is served
ok   with its content
ok   and a content type from its extension
ok   a file in a subdirectory is served
ok   with its content
ok   a binary file survives the round trip
ok   and is typed by extension
ok   an unknown extension is bytes, not a guess
ok   a symlink that stays inside the root is served
ok   and resolves to its target

-- what must not be
ok   a symlink pointing out of the root is refused
ok   a .. that reaches a real file is refused
ok   and so is one that climbs out through a subdirectory
ok   a sibling sharing the root's name prefix is refused
ok   a directory is not a listing
ok   a missing file is 404
ok   an absolute path does not escape
ok   an empty path is 404, not the root
ok   a NUL byte is refused as a value, not a crash
ok   a non-string is 404
ok   a root that does not exist is the server's fault, not the client's

